{
  "id": "80646",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Effect of Change in Temperature on Equilibrium",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Changing a concentration perturbs an equilibrium because the reaction quotient is shifted away from the equilibrium value. In this situation, the reaction shifts such that the same value for the equilibrium constant, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": ", is reestablished. Changing the temperature of a system at equilibrium has a different effect: a change in temperature actually changes the value of the equilibrium constant. However, we can qualitatively predict the effect of the temperature change by treating it as a stress on the system and applying Le Châtelier's principle."
              }
            ],
            "id": "0zrh98qdqhj2hk9",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When hydrogen reacts with gaseous iodine, heat is evolved:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "pnaw2jtp10xiwik",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "3e9voepmtqysy1j",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1wg46jguvih7tib",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm I}_2(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HI}(g)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\; \\mathrm\\Delta H\\;=\\;-9.4\\;\\mathrm{kJ}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "where Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "text": " is the enthalpy change for the reaction. Because this reaction is exothermic (Δ"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "H"
              },
              {
                "text": " is negative), we can write it with heat as a product:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "o3k7ihbmloglh0u",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "tkujrawqkl464k0",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "viljcfz1ve4mtvo",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm I}_2(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HI}(g)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{heat}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Increasing the temperature of the reaction increases the internal energy of the system. In effect, this adds heat—a reaction product—to the system. The reaction shifts to the left to relieve the stress by using heat, which increases the concentrations of the reactants (H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ") and decreases the concentration of the product (HI). Lowering the temperature of this system has the opposite effect. It decreases the internal energy of the system, effectively removing heat. The reaction shifts right to produce heat, which increases [HI] and decreases [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] and [I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "]."
              }
            ],
            "id": "gnfyp415usakd6w",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When we change the temperature of a system at equilibrium, the value of the equilibrium constant for the reaction changes. Lowering the temperature of this system increases the value of the equilibrium constant: at the new equilibrium, the concentration of HI has increased and the concentrations of H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " have decreased. For example, for this reaction, the value of the equilibrium constant changes from "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 50.0 at 400 °C to "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": " = 67.5 at 357 °C. Raising the temperature of this system results in an increase in [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] and [I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": "] and a decrease in [HI], so the value of "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": " decreases."
              }
            ],
            "id": "i1j9lbikhd5i3gm",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3667477693",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consider the equilibrium reaction between N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (a colorless gas) and NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (a brown gas):"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1cek1kll7alh8r2",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "74q420t6uhbfpgs",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "99nb6sc8lkokbcc",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm N}_2{\\mathrm O}_4(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;{\\mathrm{NO}}_2(g)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\mathrm\\Delta H\\; =\\;57.2\\;\\mathrm{kJ}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "At 25 °C, a sealed glass tube containing an equilibrium mixture of N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " has a light brown color. If this mixture is heated to 50 °C, what will you observe? What will happen to the equilibrium constant? What will you observe and what will happen to "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " if the mixture is cooled to 0 °C?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "909dsrm9v7mt3wb",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The positive Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " value tells us that the reaction is endothermic and could be written:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "02s3nrg2m0rxjaj",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "iy9mhixl0tbrk76",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "lmt0j7p8dib0lw9",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Heat}\\;+\\;{\\mathrm N}_2{\\mathrm O}_4(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;{\\mathrm{NO}}_2(g)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "When the mixture is heated, we stress the system by adding heat (a reactant). The system shifts to the right to relieve the stress by using up heat. This decreases the concentration of colorless N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " molecules and increases the concentration of brown NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " molecules, so the mixture has a darker brown color than at room temperature. At the higher temperature, [NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is higher and [N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is lower, so the value of "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " at 50 °C will be larger than the value at 25 °C. When the mixture is cooled, heat is removed, so the equilibrium shifts to the left to supply some of the energy lost by cooling. The concentration of colorless N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " increases and the concentration of brown NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " decreases, causing the brown color to fade. At the lower temperature, [NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is lower and [N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] is higher, so the value of "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " at 0 °C will be smaller than the value at 25 °C."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "k76oqa5vys0xak9",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Watch the video below that illustrates how the N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " / NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " equilibrium system responds to changes in temperature. To play the video, click the "
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "N"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": " / NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "strong": true,
                    "text": " Equilibrium Video"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " button."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wyug8be0v441vjj",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
